  <constraints>
    <constraint type="architecture">Compilation is non-blocking. A compilation failure must never prevent a story from being marked as completed. Knowledge compilation is an enhancement layer, not a gate.</constraint>
    <constraint type="cost">The COMPILE phase adds ~$0.03-0.08 per story (agent step) + ~$0.001 (embedding). The shell steps are free. Total additional cost per story: approximately $0.03-0.08.</constraint>
    <constraint type="ordering">The three compile steps must execute sequentially: compile-diff produces DIFF_MANIFEST, which feeds compile-knowledge, which produces articles that compile-sync embeds. The captureAs chaining must be correct.</constraint>
    <constraint type="types">The EpicStory type change in functions/shared/types/epic-workflow.ts MUST be mirrored in src/types/epic-workflow.ts to keep frontend and backend types in sync.</constraint>
    <constraint type="infrastructure">Compile steps depend on infrastructure from Epic 1 (wiki directory, Memgraph, graph-sync.mjs). If Epic 1 is not yet deployed, compilation should gracefully skip (compilationStatus: 'skipped').</constraint>
  </constraints>

